  "id": "COMPOUND:24046 - PROTEIN:5826",
  "verbalization": "Anguidine deriv scirpentriol is implicated in the biological activity against SMMC-7721 through a series of molecular targets, including Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, and other compounds such as Isodaucene and Phorone. These targets are all involved in cellular processes that can influence the behavior of the SMMC-7721 cell line. The evidence suggests a potential mechanism where Anguidine deriv scirpentriol modulates cellular redox homeostasis by targeting Thioredoxin, which in turn may affect the function of other downstream targets like Isodaucene and Phorone. This chain of interactions implies that Anguidine deriv scirpentriol could exert its effects on SMMC-7721 through a complex network of molecular pathways, possibly involving redox regulation and cellular stress responses. The integrated evidence highlights a recurring role of Thioredoxin as a central node in this relationship, suggesting that the drug may act through a redox-dependent mechanism to influence the cell line.",
